---The Queue Properties definition.
---@class azure.servicebus.SBQueueProperties
---@field countDetails? azure.servicebus.MessageCountDetails Message Count Details.
---@field createdAt? string The exact time the message was created.
---@field updatedAt? string The exact time the message was updated.
---@field accessedAt? string Last time a message was sent, or the last time there was a receive request to this queue.
---@field sizeInBytes? number The size of the queue, in bytes.
---@field messageCount? number The number of messages in the queue.
---@field lockDuration? string ISO 8601 timespan duration of a peek-lock; that is, the amount of time that the message is locked for other receivers. The maximum value for LockDuration is 5 minutes; the default value is 1 minute.
---@field maxSizeInMegabytes? number The maximum size of the queue in megabytes, which is the size of memory allocated for the queue. Default is 1024.
---@field maxMessageSizeInKilobytes? number Maximum size (in KB) of the message payload that can be accepted by the queue. This property is only used in Premium today and default is 1024.
---@field requiresDuplicateDetection? boolean A value indicating if this queue requires duplicate detection.
---@field requiresSession? boolean A value that indicates whether the queue supports the concept of sessions.
---@field defaultMessageTimeToLive? string ISO 8601 default message timespan to live value. This is the duration after which the message expires, starting from when the message is sent to Service Bus. This is the default value used when TimeToLive is not set on a message itself.
---@field deadLetteringOnMessageExpiration? boolean A value that indicates whether this queue has dead letter support when a message expires.
---@field duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow? string ISO 8601 timeSpan structure that defines the duration of the duplicate detection history. The default value is 10 minutes.
---@field maxDeliveryCount? number The maximum delivery count. A message is automatically deadlettered after this number of deliveries. default value is 10.
---@field status? azure.servicebus.EntityStatus Enumerates the possible values for the status of a messaging entity.
---@field enableBatchedOperations? boolean Value that indicates whether server-side batched operations are enabled.
---@field autoDeleteOnIdle? string ISO 8061 timeSpan idle interval after which the queue is automatically deleted. The minimum duration is 5 minutes.
---@field enablePartitioning? boolean A value that indicates whether the queue is to be partitioned across multiple message brokers.
---@field enableExpress? boolean A value that indicates whether Express Entities are enabled. An express queue holds a message in memory temporarily before writing it to persistent storage.
---@field forwardTo? string Queue/Topic name to forward the messages
---@field forwardDeadLetteredMessagesTo? string Queue/Topic name to forward the Dead Letter message
---@field userMetadata? string Gets and Sets Metadata of User.

